From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000002 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: husky-port CI <ci@husky-port.local>
Date: Tue, 4 Nov 2026 15:05:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] halium.config: LTO_NONE instead of CLANG_THIN

Upstream halium.config pins CONFIG_LTO_CLANG_THIN=y (thin LTO was the
RAM-safe choice vs full LTO). On zuma, thin LTO + CFI mis-links
cross-module calls (dwc3_exynos_usb -> exynos_usbdrd_s2mpu_manual_control
bound to etm2dram_probe) -> CFI panic at boot. LOS builds GKI with
LTO_NONE. Match it.

---
 arch/arm64/configs/halium.config | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/configs/halium.config b/arch/arm64/configs/halium.config
index 5350ba3beafe..222222222222 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/configs/halium.config
+++ b/arch/arm64/configs/halium.config
@@ -8,2 +8,3 @@
-CONFIG_LTO_CLANG_THIN=y
+# CONFIG_LTO_CLANG_THIN is not set
+CONFIG_LTO_NONE=y
 # bluebinder
